# UPACK: packed BCD to ASCII - A+D source, X+T destination.
# Full constructor: it has two exits. The word after UPACK is the error return; on success the
# CPU skips it (YAML for the decimal instructions: "causes the program counter to skip the next
# instruction UNLESS an error has been generated"; nd100x cpu_instr.c / bcd.c: "no error =>
# SKIP return"). Without the second exit Ghidra only ever saw the error path.
:UPACK skip_err, skip_ok is op16=0xC055 ; skip_err ; skip_ok {  # 0140125 octal
    nd100_bcd_unpack(A, D, T, X);
    local err:1 = nd100_error_return();
    if (err) goto skip_err;
    goto skip_ok;
}
